    "messages": [
      "Done. Working directory verified as the evaluator worktree; no new worktree, no commit.\n\n## Result\n\n`dist/result.json` (generated locally by the passing run):\n```json\n{\"value\":\"opus-1\"}\n```\n\n## Failed run\n\n`docker build -t app:test .` \u2192 exit 0, then:\n\n```\n$ docker run --rm app:test\nExpected a repaired value, received broken-opus-1\nEXIT: 1\n```\n\n**Diagnosis:** `value.txt` contained `broken-opus-1`. `check.mjs:5` tests `value.startsWith('broken-')` and sets `process.exitCode = 1` on a match. The failure is purely the fixture data \u2014 the build itself was clean, including the `.dockerignore` assertion at `Dockerfile:4`. Because the Pandora shim runs image-only (`local source is not captured or injected`, no worktree mount), the source is baked in at build time, so a rebuild was required for the fix to take effect.\n\n## Repair\n\n`value.txt`: `broken-opus-1` \u2192 `opus-1`. Nothing else changed \u2014 `Dockerfile` and `check.mjs` untouched, no check weakened.\n\n## Passing run\n\n```\n$ docker build -t app:test .\nBUILD EXIT: 0   (image sha256:0fb717f1d45a\u2026)\n\n$ docker run --rm app:test\nValidated opus-1\n[pandora] output ready: \u2026/pandora-docker-20260920-opus-1/dist\nEXIT: 0\n```\n\nThe passing run published `/workspace/dist` back to the local `dist/` per the configured output mapping; the failed run retained its outputs in the evidence directory only."
